  "result": "The cause is in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py:623`). It builds a `shlex.shlex` object directly, and that defaults to `commenters = \"#\"`. Everything after an unquoted `#` is therefore dropped as a comment, so `prog foo#bar` is split as `[\"prog\", \"foo\"]`.\n\nI've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-lucky-stardust.md` and haven't edited any code yet, since plan mode is active.\n\n**Planned changes**\n1. **Fix:** in `split_arg_string`, set `lex.commenters = \"\"` after `lex.whitespace_split = True`. This matches what `shlex.split()` does by default.\n2. **Tests:** add cases to `tests/test_shell_completion.py`, such as `\"example foo#bar\"` \u2192 `[\"example\", \"foo#bar\"]` and `\"example #x\"` \u2192 `[\"example\", \"#x\"]`. I'd also add a completion-resolution case with a `#` argument.\n3. **Changelog:** add an entry to `CHANGES.md`.\n4. **Verify:** run `pytest tests/test_shell_completion.py` and then the full suite. The new tests should fail before the fix and pass after.\n\nThe `ExitPlanMode` tool isn't available in this session, so I can't request formal approval. Let me know if you'd like me to go ahead and implement this.",
